-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Renegade
  Publisher   Imagine, 1987
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Renegade (1987)(Imagine)(128K).z80
  MD5         9432bbad61d76f7e2a6e1a079c0f363a

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The fighters, bikers and gang members in fuller colour with more
              detail. Source: Enhanced colours from the MVV package's older
              Spec256 conversion, painter not established.

  Changes     1.1: the game keeps its own CPU speed after each sprite update
              instead of being set back to 3.5 MHz; works on NextZXOS v2.10
              (System/Next 26.11).
              1.2: the game holds the original's pace in busy fights, and
              skips enemy moves about as often as the original instead of far
              more: the sprite updates' time is paid back from the game's own
              logic at once, and interrupts stay on while sprites load.

  Note        Known issues: pace against the original in JNext, 4 runs of 600
              game updates with the same input and the same enemy choices,
              default and Enhanced alike: overall -0.32 to +0.00%, quiet
              scenes +0.02 to +0.23%, busy scenes -1.00 to -0.06%, slowest
              stretch of 20 updates +1.7%, fastest -2.9% where the original
              itself lags (1.1: busy up to +4.48%, slowest stretch +10.7%);
              levels 2 to 4 alike, slowest stretch +1.7%, bosses not measured.
              The game skips enemy moves when an update runs late: 8, 1, 1, 0,
              5, 1 times in 600 updates over 6 runs against the original's 8,
              1, 1, 0, 8, 1 (1.1: 63, 40, 78, 3, 80, 81); 4 of the 6 runs stay
              the same game for all 600 updates, the other two part at one
              skip, at update 395 and 156. Missing: the music was not listened
              to in testing; the cheats are the archive's 128K POKEs and have
              not been played; not yet checked: joysticks and the ending;
              hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite time
   3  No death
   4  Easy fight, one-hit falls
   5  Start at level 2
   6  Start at level 3
   7  Start at level 4

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

